{ "runner": "anthropic-compatible", "model": "MiniMax-M3", "status": "reviewed", "verdict": "FIX-THEN-SHIP", "findings": "- README.md states repo status as \"Bootstrap — 文件與計劃；應用尚未 scaffold\" and plan §4 Phase 0' marks design gates closed and \"Remaining optional: personal top automations flavor; zMUD import samples\"; however KR3 is listed as resolved in §8 with no explicit deferral of personal zMUD import to a numbered phase, so the Board/phase traceability is mildly inconsistent (README links INDEX.md but no INDEX file is included in diff — missing referenced file or broken link).\n- Plan §2.5 mandates \"Traditional Chinese UI first; English secondary\" while README and architecture doc are predominantly English with Traditional Chinese summary lines; spec says Traditional Chinese first — internal consistency weak.\n- Plan §2.5 declares \"Architecture must not hard-code a single host in libraries (config/allowlist instead)\" and KR2 requires connect to ≥1 non-RW allowlisted MUD, but Phase 1a acceptance only covers RW banner; Phase 4 is where second-mud smoke lands — gap between KR2 and the earliest acceptance phase is not explicitly bridged (no sub-KR for charset-selectable UI in 1a).\n- Architecture.md \"Runtime topology\" depicts `apps/proxy` reaching \"MUD host (RW …)\" but does not show the localhost dev proxy path; ADR-002 §Decision and threat model §Modes both list dev localhost as a profile — minor inconsistency in topology diagram.\n- ADR-002 Decision table says \"phone UX honesty: Support connect + play\" and Plan §6.5/§KR6 echo this; however Plan §4 Phase 1a manual says \"phone browser smoke (desired)\" — phone smoke is non-mandatory in the gate that ships KR0/KR6 baseline; risk of shipping without phone verification.\n- Threat model §\"Modes\" lists \"Dev localhost\" with \"Destinations: Public MUDs; still block private IPs\", but Plan §2.5 says \"Localhost proxy: developer / same-machine convenience; same protocol, different config\" — dev localhost SSRF/allowlist posture is under-specified (does dev bypass allowlist entirely? if so, open-relay risk on dev box is unchanged but the threat model does not enumerate this mode's risks).\n- Threat model §\"Threats → controls\" row \"DNS rebinding\" says \"Resolve → validate IP → connect; deny if rebinding class\" but does not state that re-validation must occur on every connect (or at minimum before each new upstream connection); minor completeness gap for long-lived sessions.\n- Plan §7 \"Out of scope\" excludes \"Public unauthenticated open proxy\" but ADR-002 §Alternatives rejected only mentions it; the threat model \"Explicit non-goals\" lists E2E guarantees when mud is cleartext — fine — but does not enumerate the legal/abuse handling expectation for a self-host user who misconfigures (no runbook pointer beyond the later Phase 4 \"runbook for bans/quotas\").\n- RW fidelity: Plan §2.5 enumerates \"CSI s/u, CSI H, CSI 2J, CSI r, SGR, BEL/BS/HT/LF/CR, Big5 DBCS\" as Phase 1b ship gate; Phase 1a acceptance only requires \"Big5 + SGR + scrollback; Canvas2D; banner golden\" — but Phase 1a also requires \"unauth TCP denied; private-IP denied\" while VT minimum is deferred to 1b; risk that 1a ships with SGR-only terminal that Phase 1a acceptance itself would forbid if evaluated against §2.5's complete-control-plane rule (potential internal conflict between Phase 1a acceptance and §2.5 ship gates).\n- Plan §6.5 \"MUD server output is untrusted\" and §KR4 mention \"XSS green\" but no explicit Phase or acceptance criterion in §4 names an XSS corpus / sanitizer milestone — test plan §5 lists \"Security: XSS corpus on terminal\" as a layer but does not bind it to a phase.\n- Plan §4 Phase 3 \"Optional MCCP2; careful MXP (off by default until sanitizer green)\" — but probe §\"Telnet negotiations\" shows MCCP2 WILL is sent by server in the first packet; deferring MCCP2 to Phase 3 means the big5-banner golden in Phase 1a must already negotiate WILL MCCP2 and either DO or DONT it; the plan does not specify the Phase 1a MCCP posture (accept vs refuse) — risk of MCCP-compressed banner making the Phase 1a golden fixture non-representative.\n- Plan §2.5 and architecture.md \"Render / compute plug-ins\" declare `Renderer` interface and Canvas2D default, but Plan §9 WASM note says `codec-big5` is \"TypeScript → WASM if CPU-bound\" without listing an acceptance criterion for the swap; minor scope leak risk.\n- Threat model §\"Minimum ship checklist\" item 4 says \"no password strings in samples\" — good — but Plan §2.5 allows \"Personal RW flavor packs later\" and §7 explicitly defers \"Personal zMUD file import\"; threat model does not address the risk that a user-imported package JSON could exfiltrate session cookies via trigger actions (script engine v1 is declarative, but web fetch / http triggers are not enumerated as forbidden).\n- README.md \"Project tracking\" table links `docs/projects/INDEX.md` but the diff contains `docs/projects/2026-07-21-web-zmud-bootstrap/README.md` only — `INDEX.md` is referenced but absent in diff; either missing file or broken link.\n- Plan §6 \"Risks\" row \"MCCP2 corruption\" mitigation is \"negotiate only after WILL/DO; zlib tests\" — but the server's first-packet WILL MCCP2 means the negotiation sequence is one-sided initially; the plan does not state whether the client should DO MCCP2 in Phase 1a (so banner fixture is uncompressed) or DONT (compression active) — acceptance ambiguity.\n- Architecture.md \"Surface honesty\" table says phone has \"sessions on the go; dense map/scripting harder\" — fine — but Plan §2.5 KR6 only requires \"readable terminal, send input, reconnect\" on phone; \"reconnect\" has no implementation owner (protocol vs app) and no acceptance test in §5.\n- Plan §2.5 says \"No player passwords, session tokens, or captcha solutions committed to git\" and SECURITY.md reinforces this — good — but Plan §3 file-structure shows `local/`, `private/`, `captures/` as gitignored dump grounds in OPEN-SOURCE.md while not appearing in §3 path list; minor doc drift.", "raw_log": "/tmp/dispatch-review-log-xhoYPb", "error": null }
